        "original_id": "ae76c0db-5efe-59b5-a753-89151274772b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ladies Man (1999 TV series), The Golden Girls, Maude, Mama's Family\n- People: Alfred Molina, Betty White, Rue McClanahan, Estelle Getty\n- Topics: Television sitcoms, cast reunions, acting awards\n\nFacts:\n- Rue McClanahan was born on February 21, 1934, and died on June 3, 2010.\n- Rue McClanahan was an American actress and comedienne.\n- Rue McClanahan played Vivian Harmon on Maude from 1972 to 1978.\n- Rue McClanahan played Aunt Fran Crowley on Mama's Family from 1983 to 1984.\n- Rue McClanahan played Blanche Devereaux on The Golden Girls from 1985 to 1992.\n- Rue McClanahan won the 1987 Emmy Award for Outstanding Lead Actress in a Comedy Series for The Golden Girls.\n- Ladies Man is an American television sitcom series starring Alfred Molina.\n- In Ladies Man, Alfred Molina played a husband, father, son, ex-husband, and son-in-law who lived with a number of women under one roof.\n- Ladies Man co-starred Betty White.\n- A later episode of Ladies Man reunited Betty White with her Golden Girls co-stars Rue McClanahan and Estelle Getty.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
